WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:06.439
Hey team it’s Charlie and Walking Dead just
released a new trailer for season 5 so this

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.570
will be a breakdown of that along with some
mailbag.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:12.760
I haven’t done a Q&amp;A in a while and I still
want to do my Michonne video as a separate

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.760
thing.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.660
So that’s still coming.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:30.089
More new stuff happening this week so annoucements
at the end 

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:31.089
of the video.

00:00:31.089 --> 00:00:33.910
Here we go, just a reminder spoilers for everything
through season 4.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:38.210
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go:

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:40.910
Starting off with fire walkers patrolling
Terminus.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:46.930
It’s hard to tell just from this clip but
most of the time trailers like this only include

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.740
bits from the first couple of episodes.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.830
So this kind of implies Walkers will enter
terminus somehow.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.410
I hope you don’t have epilepsy, because
this next montage will totally give you a

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:58.410
siezure.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.570
It just tells more of the shitstorm that goes
down at Terminus.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.750
It’s all footage from the previous trailers,
but I think Gareth’s voice over is a clue.

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.890
It’s not over.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.460
I think the montage tells the story of the
destruction of Terminus.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.119
At some point, Rick and the Survivors barrell
out of the Traincar like we saw in the first

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:17.119
trailer.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:21.039
Then get their hands on some guns and manage
to blow a giant chunk out of Terminus and

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:22.039
let some walkers in.

00:01:22.039 --> 00:01:28.780
But that’s not the end of it.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.009
Gareth is seen with them in the trailer in
later scenes, so he’s traveling with them

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:34.780
for some reason.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:37.969
Possibly because of Eugene’s cure, which
may or may not be fake.

00:01:37.969 --> 00:01:42.999
If you’ve read the comics just use spoiler
tags when talking about that.

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:47.560
Carol and Tyreese were seen outside Terminus
with Judith so at some point they arrive at

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:50.090
Terminus before everything goes crazy.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.159
And here we see Carol asking where people
are holding this giant rifle.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:56.590
That looks like it’s at Terminus at night.

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:00.590
So she seems like a big part of their escape
plan.

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.469
I’d be surprised if all these scenes are
only from the first episode.

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:11.170
But it’s totally possible this big explosion
and these fire walkers happen at the climax.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:16.820
It would be a pretty badass way to open a
season that’s being teased as a return to

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.170
crazy action for the show.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:26.550
Rick keeps giving speeches in this church
about not trusting ‘them’, until we meet

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:29.990
a new group of people I’m going to assume
he’s talking about people from Terminus.

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:34.090
It’s also possible he could be talking about
Abraham, Eugene, Rosita and Tara.

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:40.110
We do see Father Gabriel’s church in the
clips from the outside.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.270
That’s in the woods somewhere, not inside
Terminus.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.940
No word on which episode Seth Gilliam will
debut in, I’m expecting the first episode

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:46.940
to mostly be localized around Terminus.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:51.340
There was a recent season 5 synopsis that
posted to Fox International’s website that

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.340
read

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:56.680
Season 5 is a story that weaves the true motives
of the people of Terminus with the hopeful

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:02.010
prospect of a cure in Washington, D.C., the
fate of the group's lost comrades, as well

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:07.010
as new locales, new conflicts, and new obstacles
in keeping the group together and staying

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.300
alive.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.980
Stories will break apart and intersect.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.510
The characters will find love and hate.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.180
Peace and conflict.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.050
Contentment and terror.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:21.620
And, in the quest to find a permanent, safe
place to call home, one question will haunt

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.620
them...

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.680
After all they've seen, all they've done,
all they've sacrificed, lost, and held onto

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.230
no matter what the cost...

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.870
Who do they become?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.290
So what does all that mean?

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.790
I think we’ve all come to the conclusion
that the Terminus people are just analogs

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.160
of The Hunters in the comics, so that’s
what I think the “True Motives” line is

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.340
all about.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.760
Washington DC is one of the next big locations
in the story.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.600
They aren’t anywhere close to that, Terminus
is in Macon, Georgia.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:55.280
So sometime during this season they’ll hit
the road.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.420
No idea if they’ll get there before Season
6.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.060
They really didn’t travel that far from
the Prison in season 4.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:05.410
The line about Lost comrades sounds like Beth,
we know her story is going to take place away

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:10.120
from the survivors at this weird creepy hospital
for at least half the season.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:16.600
New Locales includes Father Gabriel’s Church
here.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:24.750
New obstacles just sounds like them running
into crazies on the way to Washington DC.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:28.160
When they talk about the stories breaking
apart and intersecting I’m wondering if

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.850
some of them might split up after they escape
Terminus.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:35.740
Like Abraham and a group try to head to Washington
DC and a couple others go in a different direction

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.330
to try and find Beth.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:51.820
I’ll say one of my favorite new things from
the trailer is Carol here in full poncho gear

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:53.460
and warpaint.

00:04:53.460 --> 00:05:00.750
You should know that when you wear the poncho
you get a 60% bonus to your crit rating.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:06.670
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and do you think Carol rescues everyone from

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:07.790
Terminus in that first episode?

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.410
While you guys think about that here’s a
few mailbag questions:

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.470
Question 1 - Mohammed Udin asks when does
season 5 start?

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:18.060
Good question, October 12th at 9PM eastern
time for people in the US or if you stream

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:21.000
it.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.560
If you watch it on TV in the UK or internationally
I think there’s a couple week delay in the

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.690
episodes airing.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.290
Like you get episodes a couple weeks after
we get episodes.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.720
Someone from the UK please confirm in the
comments.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:33.840
It’s the same drill as Season 4 episodes.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:38.940
Question 2 - Jason Pineda asks Do you think
someone from the group will die in Terminus?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.350
No, but I do think one of the lesser characters
will die this season.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:48.540
I don’t think everyone will make it to Washington
DC.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:53.780
Question 3 - Nico Mark asks could the building
Beth is in be connected to Terminus, is it

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:54.780
nearby?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:06:00.270
I think she’s somewhere completely different,
I don’t think her story will intersect with

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:04.030
the other survivors till the second half of
the season next spring.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:09.050
Question 4 - Umesh asks do you think they
show too much footage in the trailer?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:17.720
All trailers for everything basically tell
you the whole story of the season, the episode,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:18.889
the movie.

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:24.270
I spend most of my time trying analyze things
for discussion.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:28.949
So my enjoyment of things doesn’t really
depend on big surprises in the plot.

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:44.270
I get more excited about watching the actors
act when they do a good job, but Walking Dead

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:51.930
is based on a comic that is way ahead of the
plot.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.710
It’s the same drill with Game of Thrones.

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:01.320
Question 5 - Lucy asks how do you think Rick
will react to Tara?

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:11.260
I think he’ll just be wary of a new person
just like he’s wary of Abraham, Eugene and

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:12.260
Rosita.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.639
Generally he looks like he’s not going to
trust anyone new this year.

00:07:15.639 --> 00:07:23.100
So couple of important announcements, my Michonne
video will probably post on Sunday.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.960
Tonight is Agents of SHIELD Season 2.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.160
I’ll be posting my review after the episode,
but I already did a Preview video to help

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:30.790
you guys get ready, so click here to check
that out.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:31.800
It’s going to be awesome.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.280
Lucy Lawless is on this year.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:38.740
And click here for my top 5 Badass Rick Grimes
moments.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.370
Thanks for watching, everybody high five and
we’ll meet up later tonight for SHIELD.

